{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a58d59ae1afe6d5ccfcccf87037e3e35f5241a12491897b973d598a338c11091","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler idempotency test","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py","binding_store_mod._now_iso","binding_lifecycle._now_iso","binding_lifecycle.clear_absent","binding_store.py","binding_lifecycle.py"],"problem_keywords":["idempotency oracle","clock patch","test coverage","binding operations","no-churn contract","module relocation"],"propositions":["The idempotency test patches _now_iso only on binding_store, but RP-02 S2 T2 moved clear_absent and siblings to binding_lifecycle, which resolves its own module-level _now_iso, so the patch no longer reaches those operations.","The test still passes because the no-churn contract means the clock is never consulted on a healthy pass, but regression detection is silently weakened for unconditional timestamp stamping in moved operations.","Unit-tier coverage of the clear_absent no-stamp contract exists in test_binding_lifecycle.py::test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence, containing the integration-tier risk.","The integration oracle's blast radius must be restored by patching _now_iso on both binding_store and binding_lifecycle modules."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787165876905607001,"uuid":"0171eba5-9c69-4beb-9e6e-8ed637b48068"}